{
  "protocol": {
    "scope": "Coordinate-only selection audit at four previously examined sites; no model fit or pose inference.",
    "anchor": "Verified seed-42 reference keys. Frames sampled at 10 Hz (raw annotation number 3*t+1). No interpolation. Each history ends at t0 and all three lengths share the exact person, t0 and complete 30 future points. Coordinates are meters relative to t0.",
    "complete_matched": "All original anchors with 20 consecutive observations ending at t0.",
    "strict_disjoint": "Among complete_matched only, keep earliest per clip/person, then the earliest t0 at least 50 steps after the previous retained anchor. The combined [t0-19,t0+30] interval contains 50 position labels (4.9 s endpoint span); independence across people or clips is not implied.",
    "overlap": "At gap d=35, each pair shares 5 positions at T=10 and 15 at T=20: the earlier window's future overlaps the later window's history. Two 30-step scored futures are already disjoint at d>=30. Counts refer to same typed person within a clip.",
    "selection": "The original 35-step tiling anchors the first window at the fifth point of each contiguous run. Full 20-frame eligibility preferentially retains people with longer continuous histories; greedy thinning further changes the weighting of long tracks. An annotated track start or an eligible anchor does not establish first emergence from occlusion. No pose or target error comparison is implied.",
    "manifest": "In NPZ take the last T positions/mask from history_20_xy/history_20_mask, the same future_30_xy for all T, and the desired complete_20 or strict_disjoint_20 flag. The private manifest includes all base keys for attrition checks."
  },
